# Shell scripts must arrive with LF endings regardless of the checkout
# platform. This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# would otherwise write .sh files with CRLF on clone. A CRLF script does not
# always fail loudly -- Git Bash runs the shebang fine, but the trailing \r
# attaches itself to word-split values, so a `case "$stage" in ...` dispatch
# silently stops matching and stages get skipped rather than reported.
*.sh text eol=lf
